{"duration_api_ms":7577,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"2b13980d-4870-465b-bdb8-d375da3849c5","total_cost_usd":0.0008801000000000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":696,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1208,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":881},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":696,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1208,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":696,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":696},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-5-5":{"inputTokens":1239,"outputTokens":1234,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":696,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0008801000000000001,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":881,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":696,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Withholding rate:** Under Article 10 of the US–Ireland treaty, US-source dividends paid to an Irish-resident fund that passes the limitation-on-benefits test are subject to **15%** withholding. The 5% rate applies only to a company holding at least 10% of the voting power, which an ETF almost never does. The statutory US rate of 30% is reduced under the treaty.\n\n**Who bears it:** The fund is the legal recipient and the withholding agent deducts the tax at source. Because the fund generally cannot reclaim it, the cost is borne economically by the fund's shareholders. It reduces the dividends the fund receives, which lowers NAV and adds to tracking difference against an index that is often quoted gross or with a different withholding assumption.\n\n**Practical points:**\n- The fund provides a W-8BEN-E to the US payer or custodian to certify treaty status.\n- Irish UCITS ETF investors do not face additional Irish tax on the fund's US dividend income.","ttft_ms":5281,"type":"result","duration_ms":7025,"uuid":"29a4701e-f94a-493e-bfb5-d6f6ce128f80","ttft_stream_ms":721,"time_to_request_ms":97,"first_content_frame_ms":721,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
